.DS_Store
node_modules/

# Gradle's output. The APK that ships is copied into the site repo; rebuilding
# it here is one command, so there is no reason to carry the intermediates.
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties
android/.gradle/
.gradle/

# Signing material never goes in here.
android/keystore.properties
*.keystore
*.jks

# The official EPS-TOPIK listening files. 180 MB, and they are 한국산업인력공단's,
# not ours — a learner should get them from HRD Korea. Re-import them any time
# with tools/import-eps-audio.py. The manifest that lists them IS committed, so
# the shelf is described even on a checkout that has no audio in it.
content/listening/*.mp3

# Build output. `node tools/build.mjs` writes dist/, and build_apk.sh stages a
# copy of it into the APK — neither is source, both were tracked by accident in
# the first commit, and dist/ is where the 180 MB of audio reappears under a path
# the rule above does not match. Committing that would have put 한국산업인력공단's
# files into this history permanently, which no later fix can undo.
dist/
android/app/src/main/assets/www/

# The built APK. Which one this is depends entirely on the last build — 2 MB
# without the audio, 190 MB with it — so tracking it means the repo's size is
# decided by whichever command ran last. The APK that ships is committed in the
# site repo, with its hash published beside it.
*.apk
